{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The applied-state phase executed cleanly (receipt 8c866b71bf0e470e900a15e895b2bed9, exit 0, 55 events) and confirmed the state-machine-level divergence. With the flag enabled, after healing the restarted side's store kept a LogConfiguration entry at log index 118 while its peer kept a LogCommand entry there, both sides had applied through index 121, and a client entry applied after healing committed at 121 and was applied by the restarted instance and both peers (counts 1 and 2) - so two state machines held different committed values for one log index while the cluster kept serving clients and replicating over the conflict. The control reported conflict_index 0 with both sides applied to 119. Comparisons: leadership convergence holds, surviving-entry and applied-divergence are violated, the continuation predicate holds, both controls hold. I registered the applied-state divergence as a new fact (sources apply_own_log, append_new, leader_noop and the commitment sources) and rewrote the question-level account for experiment c7465edc: conclusion violated, defect claim asserted, the old 'state machines unexercised' limitation replaced by what the receipts still do not cover (application-level detection, snapshot-delivered entries, durability and disk-backed stores). Submission validated (valid true; effects: one knowledge created, interpretation appended).\"}"}}
